claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> Draining the inbox meant asking one claude session to loop the skill,
> so the session's own judgment decided when to stop. All the passes also
> shared one context, which grew with every thread.
>
> just process-email runs the loop from outside the model. It picks each
> message with get-oldest-inbox-message and gives it to a fresh claude -p.
> It ends when the inbox is empty. claude's output goes to /dev/null, so
> control never depends on what the model prints. Whether a pass worked
> is read from the notmuch index: if its message is still in the inbox,
> the loop stops instead of retrying that message forever.
> ---
> change-id: xvnlmpwlrqonwvmusyprlolnwuyqqylx
>
>  .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md |  7 +++++--
>  Justfile                              | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
>  2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
>
> diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
> index f1d9518..5598bc2 100644
> --- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
> +++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
> @@ -289,8 +289,11 @@ the commits differ, the push failed. Fix it before stopping.
>  
>  ## Modes
>  
> -- One pass: answer the oldest inbox message, then stop.
> -- Loop: repeat until step 2 finds an empty inbox.
> +- One pass: answer the named message, or the oldest inbox message,
> +  then stop.
> +- Loop: `just process-email` runs one pass per message, oldest first,
> +  each a fresh `claude -p` given the message's id, until the inbox is
> +  empty. It stops early if a pass leaves its message in the inbox.

It should not have a loop mode. It only processes one at a time.

>  ## Missing dependencies
>  - Do not install missing dependencies
> diff --git a/Justfile b/Justfile
> index fb9938d..fb70c43 100644
> --- a/Justfile
> +++ b/Justfile
> @@ -75,3 +75,21 @@ reauthor *revset:
>  # print the oldest message in the lab-devel inbox, if any
>  @get-oldest-inbox-message:
>    notmuch search --sort=oldest-first --output=messages --limit=1 tag:inbox
> +
> +# answer the lab-devel inbox, one claude pass per message, oldest first
> +process-email:
> +  #!/bin/sh
> +  set -eu
> +  while :; do
> +    notmuch new --quiet
> +    id="$(just get-oldest-inbox-message)"
> +    [ -n "${id}" ] || break
> +    echo "process-email: ${id}"
> +    claude --permission-mode auto -p "/process-email ${id}" \
> +      </dev/null >/dev/null
> +    notmuch new --quiet
> +    if [ "$(notmuch count "${id} and tag:inbox")" -ne 0 ]; then
> +      echo "process-email: ${id} is still in the inbox" >&2

Nice login, but prefix error messages with "E: " so it's obvious.
